comments[15]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-28T14:43:01.407Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check: complete all-status searches for test-name-pattern,zero tests,linked-test no-op success,GH-982,and test meaningfulness found pm-m0b7h8 for no-op linked-test mutation and pm-4i73 for meaningfulness,but no item owning zero-execution runner receipts. GitHub issue #1138 is a later recurrence with a distinct execution boundary."
  "2026-08-28T23:24:25.479Z","harness:codex","Verification evidence: linked-test execution and connected recovery regressions passed, including zero-run negative controls; full coverage passed 8,099 tests at exact 100/100/100/100."
  "2026-08-29T02:22:16.706Z","harness:codex","Review-round evidence: filtered linked-test success now requires a recognized positive runner receipt, so a dot-only reporter cannot certify execution and fails with missing_positive_execution_receipt. Shared structured-entry grammar removes duplicated classifiers; negative controls and exact coverage pass."
  "2026-08-29T04:41:16.228Z","harness:codex","Review-round findings: CodeRabbit identified that pass 0 alone can misclassify a nonempty execution and that missing_positive_execution_receipt is not yet generated into the observable contract. Reopened for count-aware classification and contract parity."
  "2026-08-29T05:25:27.229Z","harness:codex","Final review evidence: a regression distinguishes execution count from pass count, the missing-positive-receipt refusal is present in generated SDK/CLI contracts, linked tests passed, all generated surfaces are current, and exact coverage passed 8,111 tests at 100/100/100/100."
  "2026-08-29T07:13:41.633Z","harness:codex","CodeRabbit exact-head finding: quoted --test-name-pattern/--testNamePattern/-t arguments bypass filtered-run detection and can accept a zero-test result. Reopened for normalized filter token recognition."
  "2026-08-29T07:43:04.144Z","harness:codex","Review closure evidence: linked-test name-filter detection now reuses normalized command validation so quoted single/double arguments and camelCase spellings cannot bypass empty-run enforcement. Unquoted, double-quoted, and single-quoted zero-test regressions all fail closed; 8,113-test exact coverage is green."
  "2026-08-29T08:19:35.841Z","harness:codex","CodeRabbit exact-head finding: filtered Node spec reporter success emits info-prefixed tests/pass lines, which the positive receipt patterns reject. Reopened for reporter-compatible evidence parsing and a real runner regression."
  "2026-08-29T08:23:19.656Z","harness:codex","TDD review fix: added a real Node  execution. Its Unicode info-prefixed test/pass receipt originally failed closed; receipt recognition now accepts the Node reporter prefix while retaining positive nonzero counts. Focused context-integrity suite passes."
  "2026-08-29T08:23:27.641Z","harness:codex","Correction to the immediately preceding shell-mangled evidence: the real command used Node test runner with the spec reporter and a test-name-pattern filter. Its Unicode info-prefixed tests/pass receipt is now recognized only when the reported count is positive."
  "2026-08-29T08:44:07.415Z","harness:codex","Final local evidence: real Node spec reporter filtering and quoted-filter regressions pass; strict static quality passed; full suite passed 586 files and 8,115 tests at exact 100/100/100/100 coverage; linked PM acceptance passed with zero failures."
  "2026-08-29T09:36:41.791Z","harness:codex","TDD review evidence: a successful arbitrary docker command containing bare -t was incorrectly subjected to test-run receipt enforcement. Bare -t is now recognized only on direct test-runner segments, while explicit long test-name flags retain fail-closed behavior. Focused green: 4 files, 115/115 tests."
  "2026-08-29T09:58:29.842Z","harness:codex","Verification: exact repository coverage passed at 100/100/100/100 after replacing the new bare -t subprocess fixture with a fast white-box classifier assertion while retaining black-box receipt coverage. PM acceptance passed 14/14 linked regression tests with zero failure categories. Static, contract, and assurance gates passed."
  "2026-08-29T11:50:01.252Z","harness:codex","CodeRabbit exact-head finding: positive Node spec reporter receipts accept the Unicode info prefix, but the zero-test patterns accept only hash or unprefixed forms. An unfiltered successful command emitting info-prefixed tests 0 and pass 0 can therefore bypass fail-on-empty-test-run. Adding a negative control before implementation."
  "2026-08-29T12:24:43.131Z","harness:codex","TDD evidence: an unfiltered successful command emitting Unicode info-prefixed tests 0 and pass 0 bypassed fail-on-empty-test-run and was recorded passed. Empty receipt patterns now share reporter prefix support with positive receipts. Focused graph, linked-test, command, and connected suites passed 106/106; full coverage passed 8,120 tests at exact 100/100/100/100."
learnings[3]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-29T05:25:27.756Z","harness:codex","A pass count is not an execution count: filtered-run integrity must use explicit executed-test evidence and expose missing positive receipts through the public refusal contract."
  "2026-08-29T07:43:04.604Z","harness:codex",Runner filter safety must operate on normalized shell command text; inspecting raw whitespace boundaries misses quoted arguments that the shell still passes as real flags.
  "2026-08-29T08:44:07.927Z","harness:codex","Filtered linked tests need both normalized command detection and reporter-aware positive execution receipts. Node spec output prefixes aggregate lines with a Unicode information marker, which must be accepted without weakening the positive nonzero count."
